# Build outputs
out/
build/
bin/
obj/
generated/
generated_xeo3/
race_line_twin_gen.h
# tools/ is local scratch work, except the repository backup script,
# which has to travel with the history it backs up, the tool that builds
# the starter pipeline list in assets/, and the shader pack builder's command
# line (it builds from src/shaderpack), the city pack builder's (src/citypack), and the settings exposure check with its
# exception list (every cvar is a row, an exception or debug-only), the check that the words on the rows (RESTART, NEXT START) say what the settings do,
# the check that every pause-menu page fits the row cap, the check that every descriptor set is made with the counts of its builder, the check that the car's ray traced shaders compile to the same thing after the hit shading's shared code moved
# (check_rt_hit_identity.py), and the G-buffer's per-texture material tools (census, authoring script, rules, their tests).
tools/*
!tools/backup/
!tools/gbuffer_materials/
!tools/pipelines/
!tools/shaderpack_tool/
!tools/citypack_tool/
!tools/check_settings_exposure.py
!tools/check_row_tags.py
!tools/check_menu_rows.py
!tools/check_descriptor_counts.py
!tools/race_line_extract.py
# and the one that writes the Race Line path twins into the build directory from the game's recompiled text
!tools/race_line_twin_gen.py
!tools/settings_exposure.toml
!tools/check_live_readers.py
!tools/live_readers.toml
# and the script that copies the game's recompiled helper functions out of a generated folder for the host helpers' unit test (hooks/host_helpers_test.cpp)
!tools/host_helpers_extract.py
!tools/check_rt_hit_identity.py
# the settings UI dump lint (check_settings_ui.py) and the tool that makes the real dump from the sources (check_settings_dump.py), the drift report
!tools/check_settings_ui.py
!tools/check_settings_dump.py
!tools/lfg_drift.py

